  "worker_judgment_notes": "Selected the official Colorado Springs Police Department Socrata Crime Level Data table behind the public Crime Map because it has offense-level rows, occurred date, Socrata system row identity (:id), NIBRS-style crimecode/crimecodedescription fields, and point coordinates exposed from location_point as latitude/longitude aliases. This is share-lane only: CSPD explicitly warns the dataset does not apply the same counting rules as official CBI/FBI reporting, and local controls show the official totals should remain authoritative. The 2024 feed has defensible NIBRS-style mappings for 09A murder, 120 robbery, 13A aggravated assault, 220 burglary, 23A-23H larceny, and 240 motor vehicle theft. I did not include rape because targeted 2024 checks found no 11A/11B/11C/11D or rape/sex-offense rows in this public point feed, likely reflecting public-release suppression or omission; the runner should reject the no-data rape lane rather than infer it from unrelated categories. Bounds come from the repo's Colorado Springs municipal block-group crosswalk plus local TIGER 2020 block group geometry, padded by 0.01 degrees, and the runner will still spatially join to municipal block groups.",
